=== NOTES ===

PowerShell-7 quirks encountered / reused for this prompt:

(a) git diff --name-only with one changed file returns a SINGLE STRING, not a 1-element array.
    PowerShell then treats $changed[0] as the FIRST CHARACTER of the string ('.') instead
    of the first array element. Workaround: wrap in @(...) explicitly: $changed = @(git diff --name-only).
    Same applies to git status --short. First gate run failed due to this gotcha; second
    run with @() wrapper passed all 4 gates. Trimmed and re-ran the GATE section of the log
    using $content.LastIndexOf('=== GATE ===') + Substring + Set-Content -NoNewline.

(b) .github/prompts/ is gitignored per .gitignore:83-89; new logs require git add -f.
    Confirmed by: git status --short showed only ARCHITECTURE.md modification, never the new log.

(c) Add-Content default encoding under pwsh 7 is UTF8 (no BOM); -Encoding UTF8 explicitly used
    for consistency with prior phase logs and to keep Get-Content -Raw + LastIndexOf semantics
    deterministic across edits.

